========================================================================
CONCLUSION
========================================================================

1. LEMMA 1 SCOPE:
   - Required: p ≡ 1 mod ℓ.  Counterexamples exist for p ≡ 2 mod ℓ.
   - When p ≡ 2 mod ℓ: ℓ|#E AND ℓ|#E^t simultaneously.
     → Both E(F_p)[ℓ] and E^t(F_p)[ℓ] have rank ≥ 1.
     → A split F_p-rational (ℓ,ℓ)-kernel K₁×K₂ can exist.
     → Lemma 1 does NOT obstruct such kernels.

2. COROLLARY 1 (B5 COST BOUND) — no residue assumption needed:
   - #J(F_p) = (p+1-t)(p+1+t) ≈ p² for ANY prime p.
   - DLP on J costs Θ(p) >> Θ(√p) = DLP on E, regardless of p mod ℓ.
   - The main theorem (no (ℓ,ℓ)-cover attack beats Pollard-ρ) holds
     unconditionally — it is independent of whether Lemma 1 applies.

3. PAPER IMPLICATION:
   Lemma 1 → Corollary 1 requires p≡1 mod ℓ.
   But Corollary 1 can also be proved directly (Honda-Tate only),
   without Lemma 1 as an intermediate step.
   ⟹ The paper should state Lemma 1 with hypothesis p≡1 mod ℓ,
      and note that B5 (Corollary 1) is more general.

4. SECP256K1 SCOPE:
   p_secp256k1 ≡ 1 mod 3  (verified previously).
   p_secp256k1 ≡ 1 mod 7  (verified previously).
   → Lemma 1 applies for ℓ=3 and ℓ=7 for secp256k1.
   → Both the Lemma and the Corollary give the B5 obstruction.

